.TH CATALIST 1 "November 2026" "v@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
catalist \- keyboard-driven anime and manga watchlist manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B catalist
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B catalist
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B catalist
is a modal, local-first terminal interface and headless Unix CLI for tracking
anime series and manga publications in RFC 4180 CSV files.
Run without arguments to start the terminal interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --tab " <" \fIID\fR >
Start the terminal interface on the given tab: anime, manga, stats or
settings.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ls " [" \fIFLAGS\fR ]
List catalog entries in table, plain title, CSV, or JSON streams.
.TP
.BR show " <" \fIID\fR | \fITITLE\fR | - >
Display record details. Pass \fB-\fR to read IDs from stdin.
.TP
.BR count " [" \fIFLAGS\fR ]
Emit integer count of matching entries.
.TP
.BR add " <" \fITITLE\fR "> [" \fIFLAGS\fR ]
Append a new entry.
.TP
.BR set " <" \fIID\fR | \fITITLE\fR | - > [" \fIFLAGS\fR ]
Update fields or step progress (\fB-p +1\fR).
.TP
.BR rm " <" \fIID\fR | \fITITLE\fR | - > [\fB-y\fR|\fB--yes\fR]
Remove entries.
.TP
.BR stats " [" \fB--json\fR ]
Display watch time, completion ratios, and telemetry.
.TP
.BR export " <" \fIjson\fR | \fIcsv\fR | \fIxml\fR > [\fB--type\fR \fITYPE\fR]
Dump database to standard output; \fBxml\fR is the MyAnimeList format that
MyAnimeList and AniList import.
.TP
.BR import " [" \fB--clean\fR "] <" \fIFILE.XML\fR "...>"
Ingest MyAnimeList XML archives.
.TP
.BR import " <" \fImal\fR | \fIanilist\fR "> [" \fB--user\fR " " \fINAME\fR "] [" \fB--type\fR " " \fITYPE\fR ]
Pull your list (or a public one) without sending anything back.
.TP
.BR login " [" \fImal\fR | \fIanilist\fR ]
Log in; without an argument, show which accounts are logged in.
.TP
.BR logout " <" \fImal\fR | \fIanilist\fR >
Forget a saved login.
.TP
.BR sync " [" \fImal\fR | \fIanilist\fR ]
Two-way sync with the logged-in lists; a backup is taken first.
.TP
.BR config " [" \fIlist\fR | \fIget\fR | \fIset\fR ]
Inspect or change preferences (mouse, theme, default_media, default_sort,
reverse_sort, startup_tab).
.TP
.BR completion " <" \fIbash\fR | \fIzsh\fR | \fIfish\fR >
Emit shell completion definitions.
.SH TABS
The number keys select the tabs in top-bar order.
.TP
.B 1 Anime, 2 Manga
Catalogue with sidebar filters, sortable table and details card.
.TP
.B 3 Stats
Status breakdown, totals, score and start-year charts and recent activity;
\fBj\fR, \fBk\fR or \fBm\fR toggles media.
.TP
.B 4 Settings
Themes with live preview, preferences, the MyAnimeList and AniList accounts
with two-way sync, import, export and backups.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B j k g G h l
Move, jump and change pane on every tab.
.TP
.B + - S R P
Progress, status, rating and progress steps in the catalogue.
.TP
.B Space v
Visual (batch) selection.
.TP
.B / d u U o y
Filter, delete, undo, redo, open in browser, copy title.
.TP
.B : q Tab
Command palette, save and quit, next tab.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/catalist/anime.csv, manga.csv, history.csv
Catalogue and activity history (override the directory with
\fBCATALIST_DATA_DIR\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.config/catalist/settings.json
Theme, mouse, default media and sort, and startup tab; written by Catalist.
.TP
.I ~/.config/catalist/mal_auth.json, anilist_auth.json
Saved logins, readable only by you.
.TP
.I ~/.config/catalist/sync.csv
What each entry looked like on each list when they last agreed; sync
compares both sides with it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/catalist/backups/
Snapshot backups.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CATALIST_DATA_DIR
Use this directory instead of ~/.config/catalist.
.TP
.B CATALIST_ANILIST_CLIENT_ID
AniList API client id for logging in (register one at
https://anilist.co/settings/developer with the redirect URL
https://anilist.co/api/v2/oauth/pin).
.SH AUTHORS
McKaigne <https://github.com/McKaigne/Catalist>
